# armour/<body>/skirt_bell: BELL, a kusazuri of two lacquered lames flaring from the belt to 5 px past the
# hips each side, a metal-2 lacing row between the lames (N: one iridescent band a lame), R on the hem lip;
# its dark rim continues behind the legs (skirt_bell_back), so the lampshade outline reads beside the boots.
# Generated from the FORGE-LIMBS skirt templates (gen_skirts2.py, skirts_def.py; iteration 2: the D view serves U, `tags anyfacing`); Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1 A2) JAONBRASS (A2): the lames lit gold, never a flat brown field: each lame's lit run doubled (half its step 2 to step 3) and the step-1 lacing rows lifted to step 2 on their left 60 % (bell.py).
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1) T5-T6 skirt flare (STYLE_P2 29.3): `armour.t5` views facing D/U, 1 px more past the hips on the lower half; flared copies of the replace views go before them. Generated by FORGE-LIMBS flare.py.
use person
body woman
role overlay skirt.bell
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
tags anyfacing
z 10

view D key rest origin 11 0
|...vyzyyyyyyyyxwwwv...
|...vxxxxxxxxwwwwvvv...
|..vyyyyyyyyyyxxwwwwv..
|..vxxxxxxxxxwwwwwvvv..
|.vyyyyyyyyyyxxxxwwwwv.
|.vxxxxxxxxxxwwwwwwvvv.
|.vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv.
